# Accepted/triaged vulnerabilities. Trivy skips these in the gate.
# RULES:
#   - One CVE/advisory ID per line.
#   - ALWAYS add an expiry so acceptances get revisited: `CVE-XXXX-NNNN exp:YYYY-MM-DD`
#   - ALWAYS add a comment with the justification.
#   - Prefer fixing (upgrade the image tag) over accepting.
#
# The ERPNext image's fixable CRITICAL/HIGH are mostly upstream-controlled (Go stdlib in
# vendored binaries, bundled npm packages). They are best cleared by upgrading to a newer
# frappe/erpnext patch tag (which rebuilds with patched components), NOT by accepting here.
# Accept below ONLY after triage, with an expiry, e.g.:
#
# CVE-2025-68121 exp:2026-09-01   # Go stdlib in vendored bench binary; no exploit path; await upstream rebuild
